[32m+[m[32m# GymPro SaaS - Database Schema Documentation[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mThis document outlines the SQL data model used in the GymPro SaaS application. The database is built on **PostgreSQL** (via Supabase) and uses **Row Level Security (RLS)** to enforce multi-tenancy.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## 1. Core Architecture (Multi-Tenancy)[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mThe system creates a "Silo" for each gym using the `tenant_id`. Every operational table (members, workouts, etc.) includes a `tenant_id` column. RLS policies ensure that a user logged in as a "Gym Owner" or "Staff" can ONLY see rows that match their `user.tenant_id`.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m### `tenants`[m
[32m+[m[32mRepresents a Gym or Fitness Business.[m
[32m+[m[32m- `id` (UUID): Primary Key.[m
[32m+[m[32m- `name` (Text): Name of the gym (e.g., "Gold's Gym").[m
[32m+[m[32m- `slug` (Text): Unique URL identifier.[m
[32m+[m[32m- `owner_email` (Text): Email of the gym owner.[m
[32m+[m[32m- `subscription_status` (Text): 'active', 'trial', 'expired', 'cancelled'.[m
[32m+[m[32m- `subscription_expires_at` (Timestamp): When their SaaS plan ends.[m
[32m+[m[32m- `features` (JSONB): List of enabled modules (e.g., `["members", "diet-plans"]`).[m
[32m+[m[32m- `primary_color` / `secondary_color` (Text): Branding colors.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m### `users_profile`[m
[32m+[m[32mExtends the standard Supabase `auth.users` table with app-specific roles.[m
[32m+[m[32m- `id` (UUID): Links to `auth.users`.[m
[32m+[m[32m- `email` (Text): User's email.[m
[32m+[m[32m- `role` (Text): 'super_admin', 'gym_owner', 'manager', 'trainer', 'member'.[m
[32m+[m[32m- `tenant_id` (UUID): Links to `tenants`. **Crucial for RLS.**[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m---[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## 2. SaaS Billing (Super Admin Context)[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mThese tables manage the relationship between You (Software Provider) and the Gym Owners (Tenants).[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m### `saas_plans`[m
[32m+[m[32mAvailable subscription packages for Gym Owners.[m
[32m+[m[32m- `name` (Text): e.g., "Gold Plan".[m
[32m+[m[32m- `price_inr` (Integer): Price in Rupees.[m
[32m+[m[32m- `duration_days` (Integer): e.g., 365.[m
[32m+[m[32m- `features` (JSONB): Features enabled by this plan.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m### `saas_subscriptions`[m
[32m+[m[32mTracks the active plan for a tenant.[m
[32m+[m[32m- `tenant_id` (FK): The gym having the subscription.[m
[32m+[m[32m- `plan_id` (FK): The plan they are on.[m
[32m+[m[32m- `start_date` / `end_date` (Timestamp).[m
[32m+[m[32m- `status` (Text): 'active', 'cancelled'.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m### `saas_invoices`[m
[32m+[m[32mInvoices generated by the Platform for the Gym Owner.[m
[32m+[m[32m- `invoice_number` (Text).[m
[32m+[m[32m- `amount_inr` (Numeric).[m
[32m+[m[32m- `status` (Text): 'paid', 'pending'.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m---[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## 3. Gym Operations (Tenant Context)[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mThese tables store data specific to a single gym. All distinct by `tenant_id`.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m### `members`[m
[32m+[m[32mThe gym's customers.[m
[32m+[m[32m- `full_name`, `email`, `phone`.[m
[32m+[m[32m- `status` (active/inactive).[m
[32m+[m[32m- `join_date`.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m### `memberships`[m
[32m+[m[32mPlans the gym offers to its members (e.g., "3 Months Cardio").[m
[32m+[m[32m- `name`, `price`, `duration_months`.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m### `branches` & `services`[m
[32m+[m[32m- Locations and Facilities offered by the gym.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m---[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## 4. Fitness Module[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m### `workouts`[m
[32m+[m[32mWorkout Templates created by Trainers/Owners.[m
[32m+[m[32m- `name` (Text).[m
[32m+[m[32m- `difficulty` (Beginner/Adv).[m
[32m+[m[32m- `exercises` (JSONB): Array of exercise details `{name, sets, reps}`.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m### `member_workouts`[m
[32m+[m[32mAssignments of workouts to specific members.[m
[32m+[m[32m- `member_id` (FK).[m
[32m+[m[32m- `workout_id` (FK).[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m### `diet_plans`[m
[32m+[m[32mNutrition templates.[m
[32m+[m[32m- `name` (Text).[m
[32m+[m[32m- `target_calories` (Integer).[m
[32m+[m[32m- `meals` (JSONB): Array of meal details.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m---[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## 5. Security Model (Row Level Security)[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mThis is the most "study-worthy" part of the system.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m**Example Policy: Tenant Isolation**[m
[32m+[m[32m```sql[m
[32m+[m[32mCREATE POLICY "Users can only see their own tenant data" ON public.members[m
[32m+[m[32mFOR ALL USING ([m
[32m+[m[32m    tenant_id = (SELECT tenant_id FROM users_profile WHERE id = auth.uid())[m
[32m+[m[32m);[m
[32m+[m[32m```[m
[32m+[m[32m*Translation:* "Allow a user to access a row in the `members` table ONLY IF the `tenant_id` on that row matches the `tenant_id` on the user's profile."[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m**Example Policy: Super Admin Access**[m
[32m+[m[32mSome tables (like `saas_plans`) are readable by everyone but writable only by Super Admins.[m
[32m+[m[32m```sql[m
[32m+[m[32mCREATE POLICY "Super Admin Full Access" ON saas_plans[m
[32m+[m[32mFOR ALL USING ([m
[32m+[m[32m    (SELECT role FROM users_profile WHERE id = auth.uid()) = 'super_admin'[m
[32m+[m[32m);[m
[32m+[m[32m```[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m---[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## Useful SQL Snippets[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m### Check your current user role & tenant[m
[32m+[m[32m```sql[m
[32m+[m[32mSELECT * FROM users_profile WHERE id = auth.uid();[m
[32m+[m[32m```[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m### Manually Update a Tenant's Features (Emergency)[m
[32m+[m[32m```sql[m
[32m+[m[32mUPDATE tenants[m[41m [m
[32m+[m[32mSET features = '["members", "billing", "workouts", "diet-plans"]'::jsonb[m[41m [m
[32m+[m[32mWHERE id = 'target-tenant-uuid';[m
[32m+[m[32m```[m

